<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20099" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hā^drĭa</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Adria</span></b> ), ae. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>F.</i>, <i>the name of two Italian
				cities.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>In Picenum</i>, <i>the birthplace of
				the emperor Hadrian</i>, now <i>Atri</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 24,
				10, 10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 4, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 13,
				18, § 110</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Spart. Hadr.
			1</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			Derivv. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hadrĭānus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Hadria</i>, <i>Hadrian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					22, 9, 5</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 13, 18, § 110</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gallinae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					10, 53, 74, § 146</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hadriānus</span></b> , i, m.,
				<i>the emperor Hadrian</i>, Ael.
					<i><span class="en">Spart. Hadr. 1 sq.</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Eutr. 8, 5</span></i>
			sqq.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hădrĭānā-lis</span></b> ,
				e, adj., <i>of</i> or
				<i>belonging to the emperor Hadrian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">SODALIS,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Grut. 457, 6</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Inscr. Fabr. 454, 71</span></i>; Inscr.
			ap. Don. cl. 4, <i>no.</i> 19.—
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>In the country of the Veneti</i>, <i>on the coast of the sea named after it</i>, now <i>Adria</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 5, 33,
				7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Just. 20, 1, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 16,
				20, § 119</span></i>. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>M.</i>, <i>the Adriatic Sea</i>
			(mostly <b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dux inquieti turbidus Hadriae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 3, 3, 5</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">2, 14, 14</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1, 3, 15</span></i>; 1, 33, 15;
					<i><span class="en">id. Ep. 1, 18, 63</span></i> et saep.;
				<i><span class="en">Tac. H.
				3, 42</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 16, 20, § 119</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Luc.
				5, 614</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 2, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 3, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10</span></i>; 13; 2, 4, 7; 2, 7,
			13.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> Derivv.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>a.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hā^
				drĭātĭcus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Adriāt-</span></b> ),
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to Hadria</i>, <i>Hadriatic</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mare,</span>”
				<i>the Adriatic Sea</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					5, 33, 7</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Mel. 1, 3, 3 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 4, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 7, 10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 16,
				20, § 118</span></i>; and <i>absol.</i>,
			Hadriaticum, <i><span class="en">Cat. 4, 6</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sinus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					10, 2, 4</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hā^drĭānus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Adr-</span></b> ), a,
			um, adj., the same: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Pis. 38, 92</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 1, 16, 4</span></i>: vina. <i><span class="en">Plin. 14, 6,
				8, § 67</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>c.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hā^-drĭăcus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Adr-</span></b> ), a,
			um, adj., the same: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aequor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
				3</span></i>
			 (4), 21, 17: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">undae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 11, 405</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">litus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. Hal.
					125</span></i>
			.</div>
